  "name": "Question 13",
  "problem": "Suppose we wish to find a zero of the function $f(x,y)$ in the region $[0.5,1]\\times [1,1.5]⊆{R}^{2},$ where\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-4 \\\\ x{y}^{3}-2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFill in the blanks in the matrix equation below that defines the first iteration of the Newton-Raphson process starting  at the point $[1,\\,1]^{T}.$\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"1\" rules=\"all\">\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" align=\"center\">$[$</td>\n<td width=\"25\" height=\"25\" align=\"center\">{{field-1}}\n</td>\n<td width=\"25\" height=\"25\" align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" align=\"center\">$]({x}_{1}-{x}_{0})\\,=[$</td>\n<td width=\"25\" height=\"25\" align=\"center\">\n{{field-3}}\n</td>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" align=\"center\">$].$</td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr>\n<td width=\"25\" height=\"25\" align=\"center\">\n$1$</td>\n<td width=\"25\" height=\"25\" align=\"center\">\n$3$\n</td>\n<td width=\"25\" height=\"25\" align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n</tr>\n\n</tbody></table>",
